language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find a maximal independent set of the graph: no two chosen nodes are adjacent, and every node not chosen is adjacent to a chosen node.
given n : int(1..)
given adjacency_list_dim1, adjacency_list_dim2 : int(1..)
$ adjacency_list[i,k] is the k-th neighbour of node i (nodes are numbered from 1)
given adjacency_list : matrix indexed by [int(1..adjacency_list_dim1), int(1..adjacency_list_dim2)] of int(1..n)
$ nodes[i] is true if node i is in the independent set
find nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool

such that
$ no two adjacent nodes are both in the set
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll k : int(1..adjacency_list_dim2) . !(nodes[i] /\ nodes[adjacency_list[i,k]]),
$ maximality: a node not in the set has a neighbour in the set
forAll i : int(1..n) . (nodes[i] \/ (exists k : int(1..adjacency_list_dim2) . nodes[adjacency_list[i,k]]))
